  "sentences": [
    {
      "uid": "c61f1682754b3a0897ca",
      "text": "In this paper, we report state-of-the-art results on LibriSpeech among end-to-end speech recognition models without any external training data.",
      "leaf_id": "0643b5fdbcd8ec04b00f",
      "section_id": "401d5ee160fb0d875b20",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 143,
      "score": 0.0004565269236873428
    },
    {
      "uid": "892e68f657616b0d9e0b",
      "text": "Our model, Jasper, uses only 1D convolutions, batch normalization, ReLU, dropout, and residual connections.",
      "leaf_id": "0643b5fdbcd8ec04b00f",
      "section_id": "401d5ee160fb0d875b20",
      "start": 144,
      "end": 251,
      "score": 2.2474089854291754e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "c78984f876afd087cd11",
      "text": "To improve training, we further introduce a new layer-wise optimizer called NovoGrad.",
      "leaf_id": "0643b5fdbcd8ec04b00f",
      "section_id": "401d5ee160fb0d875b20",
      "start": 252,
      "end": 337,
      "score": 1.8058518261159955e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "1304b9bd7e1836578193",
      "text": "Through experiments, we demonstrate that the proposed deep architecture performs as well or better than more complex choices.",
      "leaf_id": "0643b5fdbcd8ec04b00f",
      "section_id": "401d5ee160fb0d875b20",
      "start": 338,
      "end": 463,
      "score": 3.822911232549001e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "e094b927e5d0d697b176",
      "text": "Our deepest Jasper variant uses 54 convolutional layers.",
      "leaf_id": "0643b5fdbcd8ec04b00f",
      "section_id": "401d5ee160fb0d875b20",
      "start": 464,
      "end": 520,
      "score": 1.670142184809518e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "05e2e1211d90eb9742a4",
      "text": "With this architecture, we achieve 2.95% WER using a beam-search decoder with an external neural language model and 3.86% WER with a greedy decoder on LibriSpeech test-clean.",
      "leaf_id": "0643b5fdbcd8ec04b00f",
      "section_id": "401d5ee160fb0d875b20",
      "start": 521,
      "end": 695,
      "score": 0.00033274128340681067
    },
    {
      "uid": "135198820284c24f0023",
      "text": "We also report competitive results on the Wall Street Journal and the Hub5'00 conversational evaluation datasets.",
      "leaf_id": "0643b5fdbcd8ec04b00f",
      "section_id": "401d5ee160fb0d875b20",
      "start": 696,
      "end": 809,
      "score": 0.5757072894196594
    },
    {
      "uid": "08fe5fd03ae55e332760",
      "text": "Conventional automatic speech recognition (ASR) systems typically consist of several independently learned components: an acoustic model to predict context-dependent sub-phoneme states (senones) from audio, a graph structure to map senones to phonemes, and a pronunciation model to map phonemes to words.",
      "leaf_id": "80e5c7acaec65887cda0",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 304,
      "score": 1.68324105182435e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "2dfb7ba05461f912e7cc",
      "text": "Hybrid systems combine hidden Markov models to model state dependencies with neural networks to predict states BIBREF0 , BIBREF1 , BIBREF2 , BIBREF3 .",
      "leaf_id": "80e5c7acaec65887cda0",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 305,
      "end": 455,
      "score": 1.8058518261159955e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "982075aa3b2f442a0538",
      "text": "Newer approaches such as end-to-end (E2E) systems reduce the overall complexity of the final system.",
      "leaf_id": "80e5c7acaec65887cda0",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 456,
      "end": 556,
      "score": 1.696442651054333e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "06c9d928cbe0c23002f2",
      "text": "Our research builds on prior work that has explored using time-delay neural networks (TDNN), other forms of convolutional neural networks, and Connectionist Temporal Classification (CTC) loss BIBREF4 , BIBREF5 , BIBREF6 .",
      "leaf_id": "80e5c7acaec65887cda0",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 557,
      "end": 778,
      "score": 0.00010150383174795513
    },
    {
      "uid": "05bd15ff5236c64c7b7b",
      "text": "We took inspiration from wav2letter BIBREF6 , which uses 1D-convolution layers.",
      "leaf_id": "80e5c7acaec65887cda0",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 779,
      "end": 858,
      "score": 3.1941819764587e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "5137950a9200c08192b9",
      "text": "Liptchinsky et al.",
      "leaf_id": "80e5c7acaec65887cda0",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 859,
      "end": 877,
      "score": 5.3491328957449415e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "7b617d9bbf39c8329a6e",
      "text": "BIBREF7 improved wav2letter by increasing the model depth to 19 convolutional layers and adding Gated Linear Units (GLU) BIBREF8 , weight normalization BIBREF9 and dropout.",
      "leaf_id": "80e5c7acaec65887cda0",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 878,
      "end": 1050,
      "score": 2.7108801365572047e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "0a9877444acc85145567",
      "text": "By building a deeper and larger capacity network, we aim to demonstrate that we can match or outperform non end-to-end models on the LibriSpeech and 2000hr Fisher+Switchboard tasks.",
      "leaf_id": "33eecdeed086093ddd9f",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 1051,
      "end": 1232,
      "score": 4.5397868702434395e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "65c10d16faece0201a93",
      "text": "Like wav2letter, our architecture, Jasper, uses a stack of 1D-convolution layers, but with ReLU and batch normalization BIBREF10 .",
      "leaf_id": "33eecdeed086093ddd9f",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 1233,
      "end": 1363,
      "score": 2.0948187132262702e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "1692dacbc59fe96074ff",
      "text": "We find that ReLU and batch normalization outperform other activation and normalization schemes that we tested for convolutional ASR.",
      "leaf_id": "33eecdeed086093ddd9f",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 1364,
      "end": 1497,
      "score": 0.0005316132776684705
    },
    {
      "uid": "904859030ec00e15d5cd",
      "text": "As a result, Jasper's architecture contains only 1D convolution, batch normalization, ReLU, and dropout layers – operators highly optimized for training and inference on GPUs.",
      "leaf_id": "33eecdeed086093ddd9f",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 1498,
      "end": 1673,
      "score": 4.50445955990996e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "0105b1614aa6f4ec2ebb",
      "text": "It is possible to increase the capacity of the Jasper model by stacking these operations.",
      "leaf_id": "33eecdeed086093ddd9f",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 1674,
      "end": 1763,
      "score": 1.6187581436151334e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "45221862078070974885",
      "text": "Our largest version uses 54 convolutional layers (333M parameters), while our small model uses 34 (201M parameters).",
      "leaf_id": "33eecdeed086093ddd9f",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 1764,
      "end": 1880,
      "score": 2.195348955279121e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "baa8b2f4b618b3b77c8b",
      "text": "We use residual connections to enable this level of depth.",
      "leaf_id": "33eecdeed086093ddd9f",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 1881,
      "end": 1939,
      "score": 1.606161070132327e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "c38f008c38600fa78a06",
      "text": "We investigate a number of residual options and propose a new residual connection topology we call Dense Residual (DR).",
      "leaf_id": "94187ddd9c93de7e7635",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 1940,
      "end": 2059,
      "score": 2.0303692256510018e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "bb0033eebb0d8e575033",
      "text": "Integrating our best acoustic model with a Transformer-XL BIBREF11 language model allows us to obtain new state-of-the-art (SOTA) results on LibriSpeech BIBREF12 test-clean of 2.95% WER and SOTA results among end-to-end models on LibriSpeech test-other.",
      "leaf_id": "94187ddd9c93de7e7635",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 2060,
      "end": 2313,
      "score": 0.001980039959665187
    },
    {
      "uid": "e62059597652ef62cc0c",
      "text": "We show competitive results on Wall Street Journal (WSJ), and 2000hr Fisher+Switchboard (F+S).",
      "leaf_id": "94187ddd9c93de7e7635",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 2314,
      "end": 2408,
      "score": 0.48734553741517117
    },
    {
      "uid": "118af506ad498b2aa6c1",
      "text": "Using only greedy decoding without a language model we achieve 3.86% WER on LibriSpeech test-clean.",
      "leaf_id": "94187ddd9c93de7e7635",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 2409,
      "end": 2508,
      "score": 0.0004156894770226778
    },
    {
      "uid": "edf6d052e36c15b3f54d",
      "text": "This paper makes the following contributions:",
      "leaf_id": "94187ddd9c93de7e7635",
      "section_id": "cac93106165976edbac0",
      "start": 2509,
      "end": 2554,
      "score": 1.6571452505948057e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "32a6bb0a07a8dd04a214",
      "text": "Jasper is a family of end-to-end ASR models that replace acoustic and pronunciation models with a convolutional neural network.",
      "leaf_id": "d90bf8f4a50a038432c0",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 127,
      "score": 1.6314540139585704e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "e51fe037a788393c553f",
      "text": "Jasper uses mel-filterbank features calculated from 20ms windows with a 10ms overlap, and outputs a probability distribution over characters per frame.",
      "leaf_id": "d90bf8f4a50a038432c0",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 128,
      "end": 279,
      "score": 2.0623422291335766e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "036e31a736cf3e92528a",
      "text": "Jasper has a block architecture: a Jasper INLINEFORM0 x INLINEFORM1 model has INLINEFORM2 blocks, each with INLINEFORM3 sub-blocks.",
      "leaf_id": "d90bf8f4a50a038432c0",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 280,
      "end": 411,
      "score": 1.6187581436151334e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "ca8d967a3eccf83c58b2",
      "text": "Each sub-block applies the following operations: a 1D-convolution, batch norm, ReLU, and dropout.",
      "leaf_id": "d90bf8f4a50a038432c0",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 412,
      "end": 509,
      "score": 1.606161070132327e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "2653d99c4c66c35bb4c6",
      "text": "All sub-blocks in a block have the same number of output channels.",
      "leaf_id": "d90bf8f4a50a038432c0",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 510,
      "end": 576,
      "score": 1.6187581436151334e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "e40862097ae8d680637b",
      "text": "Each block input is connected directly into the last sub-block via a residual connection.",
      "leaf_id": "d90bf8f4a50a038432c0",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 577,
      "end": 666,
      "score": 1.6314540139585704e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "285c4856561065feb4c4",
      "text": "The residual connection is first projected through a 1x1 convolution to account for different numbers of input and output channels, then through a batch norm layer.",
      "leaf_id": "d90bf8f4a50a038432c0",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 667,
      "end": 831,
      "score": 1.606161070132327e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "f8902770d8d2961f0f37",
      "text": "The output of this batch norm layer is added to the output of the batch norm layer in the last sub-block.",
      "leaf_id": "d90bf8f4a50a038432c0",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 832,
      "end": 937,
      "score": 1.5936620247162785e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "927d0ba0205843e2cb70",
      "text": "The result of this sum is passed through the activation function and dropout to produce the output of the sub-block.",
      "leaf_id": "d90bf8f4a50a038432c0",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 938,
      "end": 1054,
      "score": 1.606161070132327e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "5e22478ef60c2864fd2d",
      "text": "The sub-block architecture of Jasper was designed to facilitate fast GPU inference.",
      "leaf_id": "da7870604e0f03e2cfa8",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 1055,
      "end": 1138,
      "score": 1.670142184809518e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "9498dc9b88f2c61b91d2",
      "text": "Each sub-block can be fused into a single GPU kernel: dropout is not used at inference-time and is eliminated, batch norm can be fused with the preceding convolution, ReLU clamps the result, and residual summation can be treated as a modified bias term in this fused operation.",
      "leaf_id": "da7870604e0f03e2cfa8",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 1139,
      "end": 1416,
      "score": 1.6571452505948057e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "90e3553deb7b2a23cad7",
      "text": "All Jasper models have four additional convolutional blocks: one pre-processing and three post-processing.",
      "leaf_id": "da7870604e0f03e2cfa8",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 1417,
      "end": 1523,
      "score": 1.8058518261159955e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "9ee119a808b2c78f2852",
      "text": "See Figure FIGREF7 and Table TABREF8 for details.",
      "leaf_id": "da7870604e0f03e2cfa8",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 1524,
      "end": 1573,
      "score": 3.21923344970378e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "e50995deb2c8ed3c22c6",
      "text": "We also build a variant of Jasper, Jasper Dense Residual (DR).",
      "leaf_id": "da7870604e0f03e2cfa8",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 1574,
      "end": 1636,
      "score": 1.9223170236538176e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "2b4a3d89fde579466f77",
      "text": "Jasper DR follows DenseNet BIBREF15 and DenseRNet BIBREF16 , but instead of having dense connections within a block, the output of a convolution block is added to the inputs of all the following blocks.",
      "leaf_id": "da7870604e0f03e2cfa8",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 1637,
      "end": 1839,
      "score": 1.644249455985452e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "c0c54bae908b8f247c9c",
      "text": "While DenseNet and DenseRNet concatenates the outputs of different layers, Jasper DR adds them in the same way that residuals are added in ResNet.",
      "leaf_id": "da7870604e0f03e2cfa8",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 1840,
      "end": 1986,
      "score": 1.6187581436151334e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "6d9ea9697dc2e3b6e370",
      "text": "As explained below, we find addition to be as effective as concatenation.",
      "leaf_id": "502bc59ea642a2a6a370",
      "section_id": "c0ae928c4e44f4c419c6",
      "start": 1987,
      "end": 2060,
      "score": 1.606161070132327e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "8e850ea7445beeb0a326",
      "text": "In our study, we evaluate performance of models with: 3 types of normalization: batch norm BIBREF10 , weight norm BIBREF9 , and layer norm BIBREF17 3 types of rectified linear units: ReLU, clipped ReLU (cReLU), and leaky ReLU (lReLU) 2 types of gated units: gated linear units (GLU) BIBREF8 , and gated activation units (GAU) BIBREF18 All experiment results are shown in Table TABREF15 .",
      "leaf_id": "ff13dad552b3daa46bb2",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 387,
      "score": 9.685608308164991e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "5d4976a8aed3c5d3294c",
      "text": "We first experimented with a smaller Jasper5x3 model to pick the top 3 settings before training on larger Jasper models.",
      "leaf_id": "ff13dad552b3daa46bb2",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 388,
      "end": 508,
      "score": 9.915273115920183e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "91227d43e1f7dfcfb326",
      "text": "We found that layer norm with GAU performed the best on the smaller model.",
      "leaf_id": "ff13dad552b3daa46bb2",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 509,
      "end": 583,
      "score": 0.0003125878098696676
    },
    {
      "uid": "ba28559dcd5cebea603d",
      "text": "Layer norm with ReLU and batch norm with ReLU came second and third in our tests.",
      "leaf_id": "ff13dad552b3daa46bb2",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 584,
      "end": 665,
      "score": 0.0006825019082634147
    },
    {
      "uid": "a9e0a9e71c82afc452b2",
      "text": "Using these 3, we conducted further experiments on a larger Jasper10x4.",
      "leaf_id": "ff13dad552b3daa46bb2",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 666,
      "end": 737,
      "score": 6.605214485464791e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "925eb8c81d8efee7c84d",
      "text": "For larger models, we noticed that batch norm with ReLU outperformed other choices.",
      "leaf_id": "ff13dad552b3daa46bb2",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 738,
      "end": 821,
      "score": 0.0006487308181403439
    },
    {
      "uid": "cb8ef0f87bc1f8987b06",
      "text": "Thus, leading us to decide on batch normalization and ReLU for our architecture.",
      "leaf_id": "ff13dad552b3daa46bb2",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 822,
      "end": 902,
      "score": 1.750292578877821e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "df89fad51ba07a44de60",
      "text": "During batching, all sequences are padded to match the longest sequence.",
      "leaf_id": "ff13dad552b3daa46bb2",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 903,
      "end": 975,
      "score": 1.5936620247162785e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "0c26f25839b78a8d0c9c",
      "text": "These padded values caused issues when using layer norm.",
      "leaf_id": "ff13dad552b3daa46bb2",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 976,
      "end": 1032,
      "score": 1.6314540139585704e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "e2bf74148cc39b70e164",
      "text": "We applied a sequence mask to exclude padding values from the mean and variance calculation.",
      "leaf_id": "b9e81debd5a7ef62dd09",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 1033,
      "end": 1125,
      "score": 2.668852957262856e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "feb4fb462cad425f56a1",
      "text": "Further, we computed mean and variance over both the time dimension and channels similar to the sequence-wise normalization proposed by Laurent et al.",
      "leaf_id": "b9e81debd5a7ef62dd09",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 1126,
      "end": 1276,
      "score": 8.415109250079663e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "cf649dc2899f5c2cf5a8",
      "text": "BIBREF19 .",
      "leaf_id": "b9e81debd5a7ef62dd09",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 1277,
      "end": 1287,
      "score": 2.0303692256510018e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "a9fdc338741e711a47b8",
      "text": "In addition to masking layer norm, we additionally applied masking prior to the convolution operation, and masking the mean and variance calculation in batch norm.",
      "leaf_id": "b9e81debd5a7ef62dd09",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 1288,
      "end": 1451,
      "score": 1.7778551863194697e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "5107c334b3a8705e4cc2",
      "text": "These results are shown in Table TABREF16 .",
      "leaf_id": "b9e81debd5a7ef62dd09",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 1452,
      "end": 1495,
      "score": 0.0002982776415551503
    },
    {
      "uid": "63f893f79efec41fbd1e",
      "text": "Interestingly, we found that while masking before convolution gives a lower WER, using masks for both convolutions and batch norm results in worse performance.",
      "leaf_id": "b9e81debd5a7ef62dd09",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 1496,
      "end": 1655,
      "score": 0.00010720880092159908
    },
    {
      "uid": "e3a4804b1e1ffb3a5b59",
      "text": "As a final note, we found that training with weight norm was very unstable leading to exploding activations.",
      "leaf_id": "b9e81debd5a7ef62dd09",
      "section_id": "492c09907b8100d267d8",
      "start": 1656,
      "end": 1764,
      "score": 3.2699273422345684e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "e15a00e62837c521629a",
      "text": "For models deeper than Jasper 5x3, we observe consistently that residual connections are necessary for training to converge.",
      "leaf_id": "351796400d834d040b54",
      "section_id": "f8d2731a3c231e066143",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 124,
      "score": 2.3007035274670075e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "12c0cbc0d3532c9275f4",
      "text": "In addition to the simple residual and dense residual model described above, we investigated DenseNet BIBREF15 and DenseRNet BIBREF16 variants of Jasper.",
      "leaf_id": "351796400d834d040b54",
      "section_id": "f8d2731a3c231e066143",
      "start": 125,
      "end": 278,
      "score": 0.00012830942637841788
    },
    {
      "uid": "5288cad22f36ff0a5d71",
      "text": "Both connect the outputs of each sub-block to the inputs of following sub-blocks within a block.",
      "leaf_id": "351796400d834d040b54",
      "section_id": "f8d2731a3c231e066143",
      "start": 279,
      "end": 375,
      "score": 1.606161070132327e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "63a28b5269203a0b8dd1",
      "text": "DenseRNet, similar to Dense Residual, connects the output of each output of each block to the input of all following blocks.",
      "leaf_id": "351796400d834d040b54",
      "section_id": "f8d2731a3c231e066143",
      "start": 376,
      "end": 500,
      "score": 1.606161070132327e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "3945b94fa3192337790b",
      "text": "DenseNet and DenseRNet combine residual connections using concatenation whereas Residual and Dense Residual use addition.",
      "leaf_id": "351796400d834d040b54",
      "section_id": "f8d2731a3c231e066143",
      "start": 501,
      "end": 622,
      "score": 1.6187581436151334e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "c6253d894706c640f9fd",
      "text": "We found that Dense Residual and DenseRNet perform similarly with each performing better on specific subsets of LibriSpeech.",
      "leaf_id": "351796400d834d040b54",
      "section_id": "f8d2731a3c231e066143",
      "start": 623,
      "end": 747,
      "score": 0.00032758429785968653
    },
    {
      "uid": "ab7fec35c4a40a80f5e1",
      "text": "We decided to use Dense Residual for subsequent experiments.",
      "leaf_id": "351796400d834d040b54",
      "section_id": "f8d2731a3c231e066143",
      "start": 748,
      "end": 808,
      "score": 5.829126566113865e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "5308f888c76817c92283",
      "text": "The main reason is that due to concatenation, the growth factor for DenseNet and DenseRNet requires tuning for deeper models whereas Dense Residual simply just repeats a sub-blocks.",
      "leaf_id": "351796400d834d040b54",
      "section_id": "f8d2731a3c231e066143",
      "start": 809,
      "end": 990,
      "score": 3.0718185454758056e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "c4271a336e42d14460e9",
      "text": "A language model (LM) is a probability distribution over arbitrary symbol sequences INLINEFORM0 such that more likely sequences are assigned high probabilities.",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 160,
      "score": 1.6314540139585704e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "507716d1a8f7a6b7ec4e",
      "text": "LMs are frequently used to condition beam search.",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 161,
      "end": 210,
      "score": 1.6187581436151334e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "8589dc8e554ba6b6fa23",
      "text": "During decoding, candidates are evaluated using both acoustic scores and LM scores.",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 211,
      "end": 294,
      "score": 2.2827997192887966e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "429f2fe873b47673503f",
      "text": "Traditional N-gram LMs have been augmented with neural LMs in recent work BIBREF20 , BIBREF21 , BIBREF22 .",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 295,
      "end": 401,
      "score": 1.8925148246037342e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "a5e95f19bb917beff035",
      "text": "We experiment with statistical N-gram language models BIBREF23 and neural Transformer-XL BIBREF11 models.",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 402,
      "end": 507,
      "score": 0.00011147903794271353
    },
    {
      "uid": "0c1654762f1690700079",
      "text": "Our best results use acoustic and word-level N-gram language models to generate a candidate list using beam search with a width of 2048.",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 508,
      "end": 644,
      "score": 0.0003935755935111022
    },
    {
      "uid": "722194e2d186abd81587",
      "text": "Next, an external Transformer-XL LM rescores the final list.",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 645,
      "end": 705,
      "score": 4.069457790466838e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "c58061a34593ad75a6c0",
      "text": "All LMs were trained on datasets independently from acoustic models.",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 706,
      "end": 774,
      "score": 3.852893541726541e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "c587b8660b6ebf99dcf7",
      "text": "We show results with the neural LM in our Results section.",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 775,
      "end": 833,
      "score": 7.54332094672397e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "f5d8611136592c6ec68c",
      "text": "We observed a strong correlation between the quality of the neural LM (measured by perplexity) and WER as shown in Figure FIGREF20 .",
      "leaf_id": "22640608ba03031b433d",
      "section_id": "50febae055271e4c8073",
      "start": 834,
      "end": 966,
      "score": 9.915273115920183e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "5ee0a7ca96d2230eb239",
      "text": "For training, we use either Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) with momentum or our own NovoGrad, an optimizer similar to Adam BIBREF14 , except that its second moments are computed per layer instead of per weight.",
      "leaf_id": "51e359c818e0eaec6d0d",
      "section_id": "97ce0769b6b7143246cb",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 213,
      "score": 1.6314540139585704e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "7093f548be073980c6b8",
      "text": "Compared to Adam, it reduces memory consumption and we find it to be more numerically stable.",
      "leaf_id": "51e359c818e0eaec6d0d",
      "section_id": "97ce0769b6b7143246cb",
      "start": 214,
      "end": 307,
      "score": 1.5936620247162785e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "3796a422f59cb62f84b8",
      "text": "At each step INLINEFORM0 , NovoGrad computes the stochastic gradient INLINEFORM1 following the regular forward-backward pass.",
      "leaf_id": "51e359c818e0eaec6d0d",
      "section_id": "97ce0769b6b7143246cb",
      "start": 308,
      "end": 433,
      "score": 1.6314540139585704e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "7d8b78211adc0e1754c6",
      "text": "Then the second-order moment INLINEFORM2 is computed for each layer INLINEFORM3 similar to ND-Adam BIBREF27 : DISPLAYFORM0 The second-order moment INLINEFORM0 is used to re-scale gradients INLINEFORM1 before calculating the first-order moment INLINEFORM2 : DISPLAYFORM0 If L2-regularization is used, a weight decay INLINEFORM0 is added to the re-scaled gradient (as in AdamW BIBREF28 ): DISPLAYFORM0 Finally, new weights are computed using the learning rate INLINEFORM0 : DISPLAYFORM0 Using NovoGrad instead of SGD with momentum, we decreased the WER on dev-clean LibriSpeech from 4.00% to 3.64%, a relative improvement of 9% for Jasper DR 10x5.",
      "leaf_id": "51e359c818e0eaec6d0d",
      "section_id": "97ce0769b6b7143246cb",
      "start": 434,
      "end": 1079,
      "score": 2.265035233314773e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "0505a163d010147431bf",
      "text": "We will further analyze NovoGrad in forthcoming work.",
      "leaf_id": "51e359c818e0eaec6d0d",
      "section_id": "97ce0769b6b7143246cb",
      "start": 1080,
      "end": 1133,
      "score": 2.3007035274670075e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "41ab7a0129a01c85e9b7",
      "text": "We evaluate Jasper across a number of datasets in various domains.",
      "leaf_id": "c904e85fac4497f0cd40",
      "section_id": "b75ecb7bf65fdc6ceb2a",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 66,
      "score": 3.347468838730701e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "16956ff87401e3afef2e",
      "text": "In all experiments, we use dropout and weight decay as regularization.",
      "leaf_id": "c904e85fac4497f0cd40",
      "section_id": "b75ecb7bf65fdc6ceb2a",
      "start": 67,
      "end": 137,
      "score": 1.6187581436151334e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "e8db0173bca961ea04ec",
      "text": "At training time, we use speed perturbation with fixed +/-10% BIBREF29 for LibriSpeech.",
      "leaf_id": "c904e85fac4497f0cd40",
      "section_id": "b75ecb7bf65fdc6ceb2a",
      "start": 138,
      "end": 225,
      "score": 1.606161070132327e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "4ca81e8986cb42bab1eb",
      "text": "For WSJ and Hub5'00, we use a random speed perturbation factor between [-10%, 10%] as each utterance is fed into the model.",
      "leaf_id": "c904e85fac4497f0cd40",
      "section_id": "b75ecb7bf65fdc6ceb2a",
      "start": 226,
      "end": 349,
      "score": 2.1112482331487176e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "b715be006ecb721038df",
      "text": "All models have been trained on NVIDIA DGX-1 in mixed precision BIBREF30 using OpenSeq2Seq BIBREF31 .",
      "leaf_id": "c904e85fac4497f0cd40",
      "section_id": "b75ecb7bf65fdc6ceb2a",
      "start": 350,
      "end": 451,
      "score": 1.9373936508326677e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "896cf200ff85207ebd54",
      "text": "Source code, training configurations, and pretrained models are available.",
      "leaf_id": "c904e85fac4497f0cd40",
      "section_id": "b75ecb7bf65fdc6ceb2a",
      "start": 452,
      "end": 526,
      "score": 1.606161070132327e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "5ee8d7287ba2b0008cd2",
      "text": "We evaluated the performance of Jasper on two read speech datasets: LibriSpeech and Wall Street Journal (WSJ).",
      "leaf_id": "a82335a9f7cbe69beb93",
      "section_id": "c1950d99bd5a390a3330",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 110,
      "score": 7.54332094672397e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "68526bed736edf222ead",
      "text": "For LibriSpeech, we trained Jasper DR 10x5 using our NovoGrad optimizer for 400 epochs.",
      "leaf_id": "a82335a9f7cbe69beb93",
      "section_id": "c1950d99bd5a390a3330",
      "start": 111,
      "end": 198,
      "score": 2.668852957262856e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "eb6a62b8c4f552b76bd2",
      "text": "We achieve SOTA performance on the test-clean subset and SOTA among end-to-end speech recognition models on test-other.",
      "leaf_id": "a82335a9f7cbe69beb93",
      "section_id": "c1950d99bd5a390a3330",
      "start": 199,
      "end": 318,
      "score": 0.0008009536125085409
    },
    {
      "uid": "234c7b0b1c632ef58880",
      "text": "We trained a smaller Jasper 10x3 model with SGD with momentum optimizer for 400 epochs on a combined WSJ dataset (80 hours): LDC93S6A (WSJ0) and LDC94S13A (WSJ1).",
      "leaf_id": "a82335a9f7cbe69beb93",
      "section_id": "c1950d99bd5a390a3330",
      "start": 319,
      "end": 481,
      "score": 0.0001063745841626834
    },
    {
      "uid": "3ba13b12135fa4529248",
      "text": "The results are provided in Table TABREF29 .",
      "leaf_id": "a82335a9f7cbe69beb93",
      "section_id": "c1950d99bd5a390a3330",
      "start": 482,
      "end": 526,
      "score": 0.00021824205527083243
    },
    {
      "uid": "f80f23b57300dcde1916",
      "text": "We also evaluate the Jasper model's performance on a conversational English corpus.",
      "leaf_id": "adfaf87dfa804aa797dd",
      "section_id": "94f729bac274c7799322",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 83,
      "score": 4.231559699903632e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "c97c104ff9262190b5a8",
      "text": "The Hub5 Year 2000 (Hub5'00) evaluation (LDC2002S09, LDC2005S13) is widely used in academia.",
      "leaf_id": "adfaf87dfa804aa797dd",
      "section_id": "94f729bac274c7799322",
      "start": 84,
      "end": 176,
      "score": 4.331903899346328e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "5153c040166bf8b314a6",
      "text": "It is divided into two subsets: Switchboard (SWB) and Callhome (CHM).",
      "leaf_id": "adfaf87dfa804aa797dd",
      "section_id": "94f729bac274c7799322",
      "start": 177,
      "end": 246,
      "score": 1.6187581436151334e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "2d79ada1f60bd5e31c0a",
      "text": "The training data for both the acoustic and language models consisted of the 2000hr Fisher+Switchboard training data (LDC2004S13, LDC2005S13, LDC97S62).",
      "leaf_id": "adfaf87dfa804aa797dd",
      "section_id": "94f729bac274c7799322",
      "start": 247,
      "end": 399,
      "score": 5.9673520701231884e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "a6ae04ff5e506566be15",
      "text": "Jasper DR 10x5 was trained using SGD with momentum for 50 epochs.",
      "leaf_id": "adfaf87dfa804aa797dd",
      "section_id": "94f729bac274c7799322",
      "start": 400,
      "end": 465,
      "score": 1.7917988275182845e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "279b077c2f9f86d8029d",
      "text": "We compare to other models trained using the same data and report Hub5'00 results in Table TABREF31 .",
      "leaf_id": "adfaf87dfa804aa797dd",
      "section_id": "94f729bac274c7799322",
      "start": 466,
      "end": 567,
      "score": 0.0010525685405347706
    },
    {
      "uid": "9634a6054d6204a189df",
      "text": "We obtain good results for SWB.",
      "leaf_id": "adfaf87dfa804aa797dd",
      "section_id": "94f729bac274c7799322",
      "start": 568,
      "end": 599,
      "score": 0.010818448652863185
    },
    {
      "uid": "82a1488350f9f5be5a44",
      "text": "However, there is work to be done to improve WER on harder tasks such as CHM.",
      "leaf_id": "adfaf87dfa804aa797dd",
      "section_id": "94f729bac274c7799322",
      "start": 600,
      "end": 677,
      "score": 2.5071593847983193e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "d199a69b9e54836022a8",
      "text": "We have presented a new family of neural architectures for end-to-end speech recognition.",
      "leaf_id": "5a808504df75a24504f6",
      "section_id": "e2805bf0ef44c35c1c5d",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 89,
      "score": 3.975192649653812e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "9bc2978e49213b01f256",
      "text": "Inspired by wav2letter's convolutional approach, we build a deep and scalable model, which requires a well-designed residual topology, effective regularization, and a strong optimizer.",
      "leaf_id": "5a808504df75a24504f6",
      "section_id": "e2805bf0ef44c35c1c5d",
      "start": 90,
      "end": 274,
      "score": 2.3187477504664322e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "307978ee5243ccbcbcac",
      "text": "As our architecture studies demonstrated, a combination of standard components leads to SOTA results on LibriSpeech and competitive results on other benchmarks.",
      "leaf_id": "5a808504df75a24504f6",
      "section_id": "e2805bf0ef44c35c1c5d",
      "start": 275,
      "end": 435,
      "score": 0.30311259225265214
    },
    {
      "uid": "77782951499768a8fdd6",
      "text": "Our Jasper architecture is highly efficient for training and inference, and serves as a good baseline approach on top of which to explore more sophisticated regularization, data augmentation, loss functions, language models, and optimization strategies.",
      "leaf_id": "5a808504df75a24504f6",
      "section_id": "e2805bf0ef44c35c1c5d",
      "start": 436,
      "end": 689,
      "score": 2.2827997192887966e-05
    },
    {
      "uid": "e7f32e7970a4c011e513",
      "text": "We are interested to see if our approach can continue to scale to deeper models and larger datasets.",
      "leaf_id": "5a808504df75a24504f6",
      "section_id": "e2805bf0ef44c35c1c5d",
      "start": 690,
      "end": 790,
      "score": 7.086326620752597e-05
    }
  ],
  "prepare_seconds": 1.0303061022423208,
  "leaf_count": 16
}